p.src:
Response: After the action has been written as $A=\int L\,dt$, the integrand is the Lagrangian. This is not only a definition: varying that integrand gives the Euler–Lagrange equations $\frac{d}{dt}
\left(\frac{\partial L}{\partial\dot x^\mu}\right)
=\frac{\partial L}{\partial x^\mu},$ which are equivalent to the geodesic equation after the parameterization is handled consistently.  (Lecture timestamp: 00:28:36–00:29:02)

